Description: omit build path remapping flags from the embedded build metadata
 dpkg passes the -ffile-prefix-map, -fdebug-prefix-map, and sometimes
 -fmacro-prefix-map flags to make the build reproducible. HAProxy embeds the
 verbose CFLAGS string into its version banner, so without this change the
 build machine's directory layout would leak into `haproxy -vv` output and the
 banner would differ between otherwise identical builds.
 .
 This is now the only permanent change the Pigsty packaging makes to the
 upstream source tree. The downstream systemd unit and every other packaging
 asset is shared with the RPM spec through the haproxy-utils archive instead
 of being patched in here.
Author: Debian HAProxy Maintainers <pkg-haproxy-maintainers@lists.alioth.debian.org>,
 Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-08-31
---
 Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -1076 +1076 @@ src/version.o:	src/version.c $(DEP)
-	      -DBUILD_CFLAGS='"$(strip $(VERBOSE_CFLAGS))"' \
+	      -DBUILD_CFLAGS='"$(filter-out -ffile-prefix-map=% -fdebug-prefix-map=% -fmacro-prefix-map=%,$(strip $(VERBOSE_CFLAGS)))"' \
